{"t": 1794105104.8352127, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 cause found and fixed in code.\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 now adds a `currency` field to every row. `reports/export.py` declared only `id, amount` in csv.DictWriter, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the request failed (5xx/502 at the gateway).\n\nEvidence: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1) \u2014 \"ERROR export failed: ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'\" alongside \"INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row\" (logged 2026-11-04 19:02:11 UTC).\n\nFix: added `currency` to the export fieldnames; CSV is now `id,amount,currency`. Rows without currency still export with an empty value. Verified locally against both shapes. A deploy of reports-api is needed to pick up the change."}, "ok": true}
